{#
	Maps to the Figma `article-toc` component (30:206).

	Ships empty and hidden. assets/js/toc.js fills it from the rendered h2
	nodes and unhides it — so with no JavaScript there is no empty widget,
	there is nothing.

	The active marker sits on the start edge, which is the right in RTL:
	border-inline-start, never border-left.

	The 2026-09 revision adds `toc-share` as a child of this component, so the
	share row lives and dies with the list: a post with fewer than two h2s
	renders neither, and `.article__aside:has([hidden])` still collapses the
	whole column. That is the composition the file draws, and it keeps one rule
	deciding whether the aside exists rather than two.

	`data-toc` and `hidden` moved onto a wrapper so the nav's accessible name
	still covers the list and nothing else — toc.js and the collapse rule both
	key off the root, so neither changed.

	Params:
	  post  Timber\Post — the article being read, for the share URL.
#}

<div class="article-toc" data-toc hidden>
	<nav class="article-toc__nav" aria-labelledby="toc-heading">
		<p class="article-toc__heading" id="toc-heading">בעמוד הזה</p>
		<ul class="article-toc__list" data-toc-list></ul>
	</nav>

	<div class="article-toc__share">
		<p class="article-toc__share-label" id="toc-share-label">שיתוף</p>

		<ul class="article-toc__share-links" role="list" aria-labelledby="toc-share-label">
			{#
				First in the DOM, so it lands on the start edge — the right —
				which is where the frame draws it.

				Hidden until toc.js has confirmed a clipboard to write to. A
				button that silently does nothing is worse than no button, and
				this one cannot degrade to a link: there is nothing to link to.
			#}
			<li>
				<button
					class="article-toc__share-link"
					type="button"
					data-copy-link
					data-copied-label="הקישור הועתק"
					hidden
				>העתקת קישור</button>
			</li>

			<li>
				<a
					class="article-toc__share-link"
					href="https://www.linkedin.com/sharing/share-offsite/?url={{ post.link|url_encode }}"
					target="_blank"
					rel="noopener"
				>LinkedIn</a>
			</li>
		</ul>
	</div>
</div>
